## Source
2026-06-04 foundations audit, TENSION-01. Three sites, three authority
structures:
- spec-erg-v1.md:9 "This file is normative"
- spec-erg-v1.md:11 "Any divergence between this document and the erg
  binary must be resolved by aligning the specification with the
  behavior."
- README.md:85 "Normative specification: erg spec"
- AGENTS.md:35 "the plain .erg file is the contract and the binary is
  optional"
No reconciliation of which applies when.

## Proposed resolution (author ratifies wording at PR review)
Three scopes, one sentence each in the spec's preamble:
- The SPEC is normative for FILES: what is a valid %erg 0.1 ticket.
- The BINARY is normative for the SPEC'S TEXT: divergence is spec
  errata, fixed by aligning the spec to behavior -- UNLESS the
  behavior violates a stated invariant, in which case it is a bug.
- The PEP arbitrates intent when the above two collide.
README wording stays "normative specification" (correct under scope
1); AGENTS.md "file is the contract" stays (it speaks of agnosticism,
not spec authority) -- add a pointer if it sharpens the read.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Authority paragraph in spec-erg-v1.md preamble (3 scopes)
- [ ] No remaining contradiction among spec/README/AGENTS readings
- [ ] make check passes (spec is embedded: rebuild + selfcoherence)
